+## A throwing `beforeSession`
+
+- A `beforeSession` hook that throws runs inside the same `try` as the rest of the turn: the caller still receives its error as a rejection, `onError` receives that same error with the same `(session, error)` shape as any other orchestrator failure, and `afterSession` still runs ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L40)).
+- `afterSession` is told nothing about how much of the turn happened: it cannot tell a `beforeSession` that failed — where no user input was read, no provider was called and no tool ran — from a turn that finished. A hook that releases what `beforeSession` allocated must therefore tolerate releasing something that was never allocated, for example by checking its own handle before closing it.
+
